Gears of War 3: mouse side buttons and wheel in the keyboard/mouse binds, and mnk_wheel_weapon_cycle.
The back and forward buttons bind as Mouse4 and Mouse5. A wheel notch is held briefly as WheelUp /
WheelDown (60 ms, then 40 ms released before the next, at most 4 waiting), so a bind can use it like a
button. With mnk_wheel_weapon_cycle on, a notch instead presses the next (up) or previous (down) weapon's
d-pad button, in the order left, right, down, up, starting from the slot a d-pad bind last selected.
Wheel input is ignored while xam_input_block is set (an overlay is open).

